        "original_id": "012275c0-3666-5a79-a702-974128e0e429",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: General Motors, Chevrolet Motor Car Company\n- Products: Chevrolet, Oakland, Oldsmobile, Buick, Cadillac\n- People: Louis Chevrolet, William C. Durant\n- Concepts: General Motors companion make program, product ladder\n\nFacts:\n- On November 3, 1911, Louis Chevrolet and ousted General Motors founder William C. Durant started the Chevrolet Motor Car Company.\n- As General Motors entered the 1920s, its product ladder began with the price-leading Chevrolet marque and then moved upward through Oakland, Oldsmobile, Buick, and ultimately the luxury Cadillac marque by price, power, and appointments.\n- Chevrolet, colloquially called Chevy, is an American automobile division of General Motors.",
